WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:04.340
As an entrepreneur you can lose many different
things.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.340
You can lose money.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.450
You can lose a great employee, a great sales
rep, a big deal, a big client, a big vendor,

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.650
a great partner.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.990
You can lose a great attorney, a great accountant.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.090
You can lose many different things.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.449
It's going to be painful.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.449
Don't get me wrong.

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:18.630
It's going to hurt.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.560
It's going to sting.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.499
But if you lose this one thing, this is the
kiss of death.

00:00:23.499 --> 00:00:24.499
Let me tell you.

00:00:24.499 --> 00:00:26.329
It is the kiss of death above all.

00:00:26.329 --> 00:00:28.009
It's the kiss of death.

00:00:28.009 --> 00:00:32.400
I remember when I was at a fight with Manny
Pacquiao, he was fighting Marquez.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.670
I don't know if you remember that fight.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.879
And Manny Pacquiao, for the longest time,
it didn't matter who he fought, you would

00:00:39.879 --> 00:00:41.719
just look at this guy.

00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:45.800
He was like a hungry pit bull.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.671
He was just ready to go after you.

00:00:47.671 --> 00:00:49.790
You would look at the guy's eyes and think,
"This guy's going to kill him."

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:54.559
And when I watched him in the Marquez fight,
his eyes were too smiley.

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:55.559
He was too loose.

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:57.789
And he went and fought, and Marquez caught
him.

00:00:57.789 --> 00:00:58.789
He fell out.

00:00:58.789 --> 00:01:00.610
I was sitting right next to his wife; his
family invited me.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:01.910
And I was right there.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.210
When he got knocked out, I was sitting there
saying, "Oh my gosh.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.579
What just happened here?"

00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:08.390
He lost his edge.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:10.170
His edge was gone.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:14.700
If there is one thing you don't ever want
to lose, it's your edge.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.930
And I'm going to tell you exactly what your
edge is.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:23.210
Look, many, many years ago, I was competing
in a financial services firm, and I was going

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:24.210
against this girl.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:28.290
When I went to Chicago, and these guys started
saying things about this one girl and this

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:29.290
one other guy.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.290
You know, "this girl.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.389
. . this guy.

00:01:31.389 --> 00:01:32.389
. ." all of this other stuff.

00:01:32.389 --> 00:01:33.389
And I said, "You know what?

00:01:33.389 --> 00:01:38.000
I've been around the marketplace for such
a long time, now as an entrepreneur.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.280
I've seen the most impressive guys, speak
very well, incredible background.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:49.979
Ridiculous degrees, from the most flamboyant
universities with names and Yale and Ivy and

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:52.149
Harvard and all this type of mess.

00:01:52.149 --> 00:01:58.140
I've seen them great last names, great families,
great market, great pedigree, incredible wife,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.060
incredibly good looking, well-spoken, sharp.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.229
I've seen every single thing.

00:02:03.229 --> 00:02:07.320
I would say, "this guy's impressive."

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:13.200
Until eventually I realized, having been in
business a long time, I got up on stage and

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.790
said, "Look, this girl's sharp, she's got
a lot of things going on."

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:17.970
That was my opening line.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:23.880
"But there is one thing she's missing, that
she will know in the next 3-5 years."

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.280
After my talk everyone wanted to know the
one thing.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.720
And I didn't tell anyone what the one thing
was.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.200
One thing she's missing.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:39.340
And I knew, because as an entrepreneur, as
an athlete, you see it so many times.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.819
The moment this goes is the kiss of death.

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:45.750
And that edge is your energy.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:50.330
When your energy goes, everything goes.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:51.330
Everything goes.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.730
I did a video a couple of weeks ago about
the two different things that you have to

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:54.890
have as an entrepreneur.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:03:00.299
I talked about the leadership fatigue factor,
and the leadership endurance factor.

00:03:00.299 --> 00:03:04.970
Fatigue, you get tired too early, and endurance,
you can't last too long, stamina.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:05.970
So how do you create this?

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.520
Because when you're an entrepreneur and you
want to come out with the ideas, and all of

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.560
a sudden, it's late, it's late, it's late,
it's late (yawn).

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.670
. . you're not coming up with ideas any more
because you're tired.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.090
So you're energy's lows.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.989
It's not producing ideas any more.

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:23.270
So if this energy goes, you lose your edge.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.209
100% you lose your edge.

00:03:25.209 --> 00:03:29.660
If you're in war, and you're at the enemy
lines, and all of a sudden your energy is

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:34.420
down, you're tired, even if you're tired,
to protect your buddy, he gets shot and is

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.420
gone.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.129
Even if you're tired, and you look this way,
boom, somebody hits you and you're gone.

00:03:38.129 --> 00:03:41.440
Even if you're too tired and all of a sudden
you're getting up like this, boom!

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.280
They hit your helmet and you're gone.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:48.080
It's the same exact thing with business.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.110
You've got to have these things up.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:50.790
You've got to be ready to have that idea.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.300
You've got to be ready to have that energy.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:56.040
So there are certain signs when you look at
it and the first thing I can tell you is this.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:01.530
I had one of my good friends who flew in and
he and I were sitting and talking and I sat

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:06.020
him in the car, and we were driving and the
last thing asked him before we left the car,

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.820
I said, "Let me ask you a question.

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.329
How is your energy?"

00:04:10.329 --> 00:04:13.030
And he said, "What do you mean?"

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:15.040
I said, "How is your energy?"

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.040
And immediately, he gave me this answer.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.520
He said, "Oh yeah, you know, I just started
working out and I just started this."

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.140
And by the way, I love this guy.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.160
He's family to me.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:25.760
And if he's watching this, he knows who he
is.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.850
And I said, "He knows his energy is gone."

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.860
He knows it's not the best it's been.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:37.330
He knows he's let his energy go away and he
feels it.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:42.040
The moment this energy thing you let loose,
which has a lot to do with what?

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:47.730
Diet, food, exercise, edge, all these -- the
moment you let that go -- listen, let me tell

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:48.850
you.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:54.350
There are no feelings in the world of competition.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:59.990
You better believe that Oklahoma State that
just beat San Antonio Spurs, they do not feel

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:01.610
sorry for Tim Duncan.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:05.150
I guarantee you that they're not feeling sorry
for Tim Duncan.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:10.910
And I guarantee you, when Tim Duncan beat
out a bunch of other teams who were older

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.700
and he was younger, I guarantee you that he
doesn't feel sorry.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:18.450
In a world of competition, if your energy
goes, everything goes with your edge.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.450
Everything goes.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:23.080
And I know one thing that has always been
honest to me.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.380
You know when you play the game of poker?

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:28.610
One of the best things about playing a game
of poker, playing a game of blackjack is purely

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:29.610
math.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:30.620
If you know math, you're going to do good
in blackjack.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.560
If you're not good in math, you're not going
to do good in blackjack.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:40.280
For instance, sitting on a soft 17, even if
you've got a 16 and if the house is showing

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:46.360
17, and he's got a 7 showing at the top and
you've got a 6, do you hit?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.360
Do you stay?

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.610
If he's got a face and you've got a 6, do
you stay?

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.360
What do you do with that?

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.120
You've got to hit it because it's math.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.750
So blackjack is a lot of mathematical type
of a game.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:01.090
But the reason why poker is so famous, so
popular is because you're going against another

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.720
person, and it's the eyes.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.520
The eyes tell you everything about energy.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:10.370
The eyes tell you every single thing you can
think about of energy.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.030
So let me tell you what energy looks like.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:15.510
When energy is high, ideation is high.

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:18.640
When energy is high, sales is high.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:22.810
When energy is high, your spirit of competition
is high.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:26.970
Think about it when you talk to somebody who
is 80 years old.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.350
A grandfather.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:29.350
Ask them questions.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.440
They'll generally say something like this.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.410
"Oh yeah, you know, it's great, it's fine."

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.910
Why are they like that?

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:40.930
Is it because they're now very, very wise
and they're no longer competitive?

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:41.930
No!

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:50.220
I knew an 88, 89-year old CEO of MGM who was
still doing deals at 90 years old.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.230
But he exercised and did all this other stuff
because he had his edge.

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:54.230
He had his energy.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:58.370
John Wooden was 99 years old, and was still
coaching people because he had his energy.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:04.240
If you let your energy go, you completely
lose your spirit of competition.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:05.580
You don't want to compete any more.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:06.700
You're tired.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:10.900
When people don't want to have a business
or be an entrepreneur, "Oh, you guys are just

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.190
too competitive."

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:13.510
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:15.090
You've lost your energy, sir.

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.500
You've lost your energy.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:18.790
You've lost your edge.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:22.640
Because there was a time when you were 8 years
old, and you better believe that you were

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:23.640
competitive.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:24.640
What happened?

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.300
I've got 2 boys and they're competing all
the time.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.190
I didn't teach them competition.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:29.840
They're competing all the time.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:30.840
You know why?

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.030
Their energy is high.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:33.030
They're competing.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:34.230
I'm going to do it faster.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:35.230
I'm going to do this.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.230
I'm going to do that.

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.870
When I energy goes, we become wise.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.300
We're no longer competitive.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:40.300
Nonsense!

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.240
You lost your edge is what you've lost.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.990
You need your edge back.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.850
You've got to get your groove back.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:49.080
You've got to get your grove back is what
you've got to get.

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:50.250
You can do it.

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.330
You lose your sense of urgency.

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.830
Oh we can do it tomorrow.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:53.830
Energy's gone.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:55.980
Oh, we'll do it next week.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.020
Energy's gone.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:58.050
Oh, later.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.080
Energy's gone.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.080
Oh.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.080
. . energy's gone.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.080
There's no more urgency.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.080
Energy's gone.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:04.530
And then drive.

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:05.530
You lose your drive.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:07.600
There's no longer that drive to get stuff
done.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:08.600
Ambition's gone.

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:09.690
You don't have that any more.

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.110
You don't feel it any more.

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:15.080
You'll see a lot of times when somebody loses
their edge, they lose their energy, standards

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.080
drop.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:17.900
Expectations drop.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.790
Level of performance drops.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:23.360
You don't have the same standards of people
because your own personal standards have dropped.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:27.030
The moment your own personal standards have
dropped, you can't hold other people at high

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.030
standards.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:31.240
The moment your own personal standards, personal
expectations have dropped, you can't hold

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.890
other people at that level of expectation.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:33.930
You just cannot.

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:36.800
The moment yours is high, you can raise everybody
else's.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.440
You know, just recently Toronto Raptors were
playing the Miami Heat.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:40.890
I wanted Miami Heat to win.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:41.890
Why?

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.470
Because I wanted Kawhi to face LeBron.

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:46.300
It would have been a good match up.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:53.790
But there was one game where Lowry played,
and he was doing terrible, just terrible,

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.480
back to back.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:09:00.050
Every channel you watched, he's not doing
this, he's not doing that.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:02.840
That night, the game is over.

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:05.700
It's dark at the arena.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.870
Everyone's out of the stadium, the cleaning
crew.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:08.870
Everybody's gone.

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:13.270
The lights are left on a little bit, and there
was one guy shooting shots for a couple of

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:14.270
hours.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:15.270
His name was Lowry.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:16.400
He's shooting shots.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:20.790
He's practicing his 3-point shot because it's
not going in.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:21.990
You know what happens in game 7?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.590
They win; he scored 35, 36 points and they
won the game.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:27.950
See, that is, I'm going to get better tonight.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.850
I'm going to raise my expectation tonight.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:37.500
And they win the series because of him.

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:38.500
That's the edge.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:42.320
The energy when you have it, you lift everybody
up when your energy is high.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.390
If your energy is low, you cannot elevate
anybody around you.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.520
That's your edge that you've got.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:59.560
Now, a couple of things to keep in mind.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:05.640
When you go to Las Vegas, you see the wind
turbines.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:11.140
And what they're doing is they're turning
potential energy into energy.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:16.750
If they're not turning, you see this in Vegas
and Palm Springs, you can sit there and do

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:17.750
nothing with it.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.190
There's no energy being created.

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:24.000
But because these things are turning, turning,
turning, they're producing energy, electricity

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.270
for the entire city.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:28.690
That's energy being created.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:32.580
You and your people around you have potential
energy.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:35.690
A leader brings out the energy.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:38.530
But the leader leads with the energy.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:43.450
The leader has the edge, and they feel it.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.310
Everybody around you feels your edge.

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:51.300
You don't think they do, but everybody around
you feels your edge.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:52.810
Every single person.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.310
Every single person sees your edge.

00:10:55.310 --> 00:11:01.740
So this is why when I mentor or coach somebody,
I remember one time me and a couple of our

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:09.320
friends, we were in San Diego and were having
dinner at this real nice restaurant.

00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:16.070
We were right by the water and were having
dinner and were talking.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:19.760
I mentored these guys, a couple out of Houston,
quality people.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:24.290
And they said, "Pat, you know, we just want
to be the biggest, we want to be this.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.330
we want to be that."

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:30.360
I said, "Listen, you've never made a quarter
million dollars or a half a million dollars.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:32.490
How do you know that?

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:33.820
You don't know it yet."

00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:37.690
We're going to learn if this is all about
money for you or not.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:38.690
"No it's not."

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.150
We'll find out.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:41.440
We will find out.

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:43.560
Because I've seen a lot of guys that talk.

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:46.320
Now they're continually growing themselves.

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:50.400
Like a better diet, look better, reading non
stop, their faith is incredible.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:51.760
They have their edge.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:54.550
Their energy is definitely up here.

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:57.860
But I look at a lot of people and the moment
they hit a certain income milestone, they

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:58.860
slow down.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:02.990
Because it was never about them winning and
being the best ever.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:03.990
It wasn't about purpose.

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:05.410
It was just about money.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:06.540
You see them slowing down.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:08.170
You see them getting casual.

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:10.050
You see them not improving any more.

